  "format_version": 2,
  "model_role_invocations": [
    {
      "log_path": "stages/optimize/work/.kernelgen/claude-runtime.log",
      "log_sha256": "a4ffdb720288319edfdd56b837688e595b7b57aa901216668407728a3df6c55f",
      "character_offset": 373215,
      "tool_use_id": "call_00_F65p3vj3FgJ2tGx5P75k4182",
      "arguments": {
        "description": "Profile round 2 on target",
        "prompt": "Profile the immutable round 2 snapshot of the KernelGen workspace for operator xlogy_scalar_tensor (Ascend910B4 target).\n\nUse round_num = 2 with the profile tools (get_profile_context / profile_workloads / record_profile_analysis). The candidate is a self-contained Triton elementwise kernel: out = scalar * log(other), fp32 math, output dtype = input dtype, launched through the compiled Ascend launcher.\n\nPriorities for the analysis:\n1. xlogy_scalar_tensor-timing-11 (fp32, shape 4096x4096): the candidate measures 0.1037 ms vs reference 0.1204 ms (1.16x). Our chosen tile is BLOCK=8192 elements per program with 2048 programs. Determine from the hardware counters whether this kernel is limited by MTE2/MTE3 movement, by vector (transcendental) execution, or by per-program/scheduling overhead, and whether a larger 4-byte tile (16384 elements, 64 KiB source + result staged in UB) or a different program count would plausibly help.\n2. xlogy_scalar_tensor-timing-3 (fp16, 4096x4096, BLOCK=16384, 1024 programs): candidate measures 0.0428 ms. State the measured physical bytes / effective rate and whether it is already at the achievable movement limit for 2-byte data on this device.\n3. xlogy_scalar_tensor-timing-8 and -timing-10 (fp32, 1024 and 1048576 elements): candidate measures 0.0291/0.0293 ms against a reference of 0.0267/0.0269 ms. Report the device kernel duration versus the full call, so we know how much of the per-call time is device work versus host dispatch.\n\nReport concrete numbers (kernel duration, MTE2/MTE3/vector utilization or busy time, physical bytes if available) and scope each statement to the workload it came from. Then give exactly one actionable next experiment for the Coder, ranked by expected geo_mean effect, keeping in mind that the nine small workloads (1024..1048576 elements) dominate the geometric mean and are host-dispatch bound, while the three 4096x4096 workloads are device bound.",
